BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lincoln’s Declaration of Independence: The Pursuit of Happiness 
 in the Company of Friends
DTSTART:20260909T170000
DTEND:20260909T183000
DTSTAMP:20260829T144739Z
UID:05a97461d79fa8f75a80e4adc86841@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Abraham Lincoln is justly known as a proponent of the rights e
 nshrined in the Declaration of Independence. But he understood these as en
 tirely compatible with the system of majority rule encoded in the Constitu
 tion. In this lecture\, President Greg Weiner\, a political scientist and 
 author of Old Whigs: Burke\, Lincoln\, and the Politics of Prudence\, will
  explore that compatibility and what it means for our understanding of the
 se issues today. This event is sponsored by the President’s Office.\n\nS
 ource: Assumption University\nEvent page: https://www.assumption.edu/news-
 and-events/events/lincolns-declaration-of-independence-the-pursuit-of-happ
 iness-in-the-company-of-friends
LOCATION:Curtis Performance Hall\, Tsotsis Family Academic Center\, 500 Sa
 lisbury Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/lincolns-declaration
 -of-independence-the-pursuit-of-happiness-in-the-company-of-friends
END:VEVENT
