BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Banking 101: Orientation to the U.S. Banking System (2nd Occurance
 )
DTSTART:20260922T220000
DTEND:20260922T231500
DTSTAMP:20260829T144739Z
UID:46481870fb15efbe914bd84c009c4e@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:New to the U.S. banking system? Or just want to make sure you
 ’re using your bank accounts wisely? Learn the basics of how banking wor
 ks in the United States and how to choose and use the accounts that fit yo
 ur needs. We’ll cover checking and savings accounts\, debit cards\, bank
  fees\, ATMs\, direct deposit\, checks\, and transferring money—plus imp
 ortant things to know about keeping your money safe. You’ll leave with a
  better understanding of: ● Checking vs. savings accounts ● Common ban
 king fees and how to avoid them ● Debit cards\, ATMs\, and direct deposi
 t ● Checks and other ways to access your money ● Sending and receiving
  money in the U.S. and internationally ● Questions to ask when choosing 
 a bank or credit union Meeting Link: TBD --- Event Details: https://mywpi.
 wpi.edu/rsvp?id=403495\n\nSource: Worcester Polytechnic Institute\nEvent p
 age: https://mywpi.wpi.edu/rsvp?id=403495
LOCATION:Online Event
URL:https://mywpi.wpi.edu/rsvp?id=403495
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bringing In the Bystander 2026 - Brooks Hall 2nd Floor Central
DTSTART:20260922T230000
DTEND:20260923T003000
DTSTAMP:20260829T144739Z
UID:9117b902449af0e08852a4d054d806@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Required Training for First-Year and New Transfer Students All
  first-year students and new transfer students are required to attend Brin
 ging in the Bystander. This is a 90-minute interactive training led by our
  Relationship Peer Educators (RPEs)\, who are fellow students trained to f
 acilitate these important conversations. During the session\, you will lea
 rn practical ways to step in and support others in situations involving se
 xual violence\, harassment\, or discrimination. The training focuses on ho
 w we can look out for one another and help create a safer\, more caring ca
 mpus community. At Holy Cross\, being “people for and with others” is 
 part of who we are. This training is one way we put that commitment into p
 ractice. --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152250\n\n
 Source: College of the Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/
 rsvp?id=2152250
LOCATION:Hogan 320\, The College of the Holy Cross\, Hogan Campus Center- 
 Suite 506\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152250
END:VEVENT
