SUMMARY:Bringing In the Bystander 2026 - Brooks Hall 3rd Floor West
DTSTART:20261006T230000
DTEND:20261007T003000
DTSTAMP:20260829T144739Z
UID:3c4d426f322eaa4ded0ae092a79b1f@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Required Training for First-Year and New Transfer Students All
  first-year students and new transfer students are required to attend Brin
 ging in the Bystander. This is a 90-minute interactive training led by our
  Relationship Peer Educators (RPEs)\, who are fellow students trained to f
 acilitate these important conversations. During the session\, you will lea
 rn practical ways to step in and support others in situations involving se
 xual violence\, harassment\, or discrimination. The training focuses on ho
 w we can look out for one another and help create a safer\, more caring ca
 mpus community. At Holy Cross\, being “people for and with others” is 
 part of who we are. This training is one way we put that commitment into p
 ractice. --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152254\n\n
 Source: College of the Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/
 rsvp?id=2152254
LOCATION:Hogan 320\, The College of the Holy Cross\, Hogan Campus Center- 
 Suite 506\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152254
END:VEVENT
